@node Part01 "Introduction To DMSDescript-EXEDescript by Re/Y\o/TLS/MST "

                              .: Introduction :.
                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Well it is very easy ... DMSDescript-EXEDescript can be used to make life
easier for the once that want to add, remove, extract the FileDescription to
DMS-Archives and to EXEcutables ... They can be used from Shell,
Diskmaster2.x, DirOpus, or any other DirUtil ...

@endnode
@node Part02 "Requirements"

                              .: Requirements :.
                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

All you need is an ©Amiga, DMSDescript, EXEDescript ... Some Archives ...
If you find any BUGS or have some SUGGESTIONS please leave me a messy ... You
will most certainly be able to find me at @{" Diabolo " Link Diabolo}.


@endnode
@node Part03 "How To Install DMSDescript-EXEDescript by Re/Y\o/TLS/MST"

                            .:Installation Guide:.
                            ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The Program runs on most amiga configurations ... there shouldn't be much
limitations ... except not enough diskspace ... not enough ram ... but it
doesn't consume much itself ... it's just the archives that might consume
some space ...
Just copy the programs where you like them to be and where they can be found
by FileID v1.3+ ...

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
DMSDescript v1.1 By Re/Y\\o(/Y\\ystic/X-DeSign)


Usage: DMSDescript <a|x|d> [<Description>] <DMS Archive>
       a Add FileDescription
       x Extract FileDescription
       d Delete FileDescription

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
EXEDescript v1.0 By Re/Y\\o(/Y\\ystic/X-DeSign)


Usage: EXEDescript <a|x|d> [<Description>] <Executable>
       a Add FileDescription
       x Extract FileDescription
       d Delete FileDescription

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The Description will only be used in case of 'a' and 'x' i.e. Add a description
to an archive or extract it from one ...

There is not much to say about it ... just that the description does not need
to be named File_ID.Diz ... doesn't matter what name it has ...

@endnode
